  "_harness": "__alloca_probe is a stub here, so ESP stays at EBP and the 0x1128-byte frame overlaps the call stack (timeText at EBP-0x28 gets the pushed args; server at EBP-4 is the saved EBX slot). So strcpy/strlen/sprintf/strcat/fopen/fprintf are scripted (nothing may write the overlapped stack but the stubs' `writes`); strncpy is passthrough (its dest EBP-4 is above ESP). strlen's scripted length picks the byte tested for '\\n': len 0x35 -> EBP+0x0C (low byte of a1), len 0x36 -> EBP+0x0D (second byte of a1), len 0x31 -> EBP+8.. (format pointer low byte, never 0x0A).",
